+Go 1.22 library. `Collect` owns the supplied cursor and returns every scanned
+string. `CollectMatching(rows, keep)` returns only scanned strings accepted by
+`keep`; a nil filter accepts all strings. Both preserve cursor order and return
+the successfully collected prefix with a scan or iteration error.
+
+Both functions close the cursor once on every path. Close is best-effort and its
+error is ignored; it cannot invalidate already read rows. Scan and iteration
+errors are returned. The filter cannot return an error. No retry or full-input
+buffering is needed. No database dependency.
